invariant: INV-14
file: quic_config.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: quic_config_ok takes a PSK identity one byte past CH_TICKET_ID_MAX,
  the bound hello_build proves the ClientHello in q->t.tx holds, so a
  configuration ch_quic_init accepts can make a hello that does not fit.
  bin/quic_driver_test requires CH_EINVAL and nothing staged for an
  identity of CH_TICKET_ID_MAX + 1 bytes.

--- old
    return len >= 1 && len <= CH_TICKET_ID_MAX;
--- new
    return len >= 1 && len <= CH_TICKET_ID_MAX + 1;
